# ================= BEFORE =================
h1('Before Working With Us, Nobody Clicked His Thumbnails')
para('Before we started, the channel ran on daily market analysis. He did 19 of them in the six weeks before the change, about 31 minutes each.')
para("Here's what one of the thumbnails looked like:")
img('before_thumb.jpg', 4.5)
para("Yep. That's a screenshot from the video. You can literally read the URL bar.")
para('**Those 19 videos averaged 1,051 views.**')
para('And look, the content was fine. It was technical, and it was built to sell. But nobody was going to click on that.')
para('Every thumbnail has two jobs, and this one did neither of them.')
para('**Job 1: stop the scroll.**')
para("People scroll YouTube on autopilot. Something has to make their thumb stop. The things that do it best are a big face, a big number, money, danger, strong emotion, and bright colours that stand out from everything around them.")
img('pattern.jpg', 6.0, caption='(The things that are proven to stop the scroll.)')
para('**Job 2: make them curious.**')
